---
import StudioLayout from '../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
import { studio } from '../../src/data/studio';
---
<StudioLayout title="Contact privacy — Blum Studios" description="How Blum Studios handles project inquiries." path="/privacy">
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="contact-privacy studio-width">
    <a href="/contact">Back to contact</a>
    <h1>Contact privacy</h1>
    <p>Jordan Blum runs Blum Studios. The contact form collects your name, email address and message so he can respond to your inquiry. Sending a message does not subscribe you to marketing.</p>
    <p>Messages are stored in a separate private table in the existing Chicks of NYC database, hosted by Neon. Vercel handles the website and form service. The service uses a temporary keyed hash of your network address to limit spam; it does not save your raw address with your message.</p>
    <p>Inquiries are kept as needed to handle the conversation. To request access or deletion, email <a href={`mailto:${studio.contactEmail}`}>{studio.contactEmail}</a>. Email sent to this address is forwarded through Squarespace to Jordan’s Gmail inbox.</p>
    <p>This form does not sell your information, enroll you in another app or send your message to advertising platforms.</p>
  </main>
</StudioLayout>
<style>
  .contact-privacy { max-width: 42rem; padding-block: 3rem 6rem; }
  .contact-privacy > a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; }
  h1 { font: 600 clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4rem)/1.1 Chillax, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.05em; margin-block: 2rem !important; }
  p + p { margin-top: 1.25rem !important; }
</style>
